Tests: OOM policy 25 -> 29; new terminal adjustment 5; unchanged recovery 6, terminal OOM 16, scope failure 7, path completion 2. Consumer sweep: 165 files, 4278 passed, 66 skipped, 0 failed. scripts/check: 20 checks passed.
RED: bound-interpreter and dispatcher regressions fail without process-set matching; real LocalEnvironment commands report 200 rather than 1000 without prefixing. Nine mutations killed: dropped bound IDs, dropped launcher, foreign task/run acceptance, invalid PIDs, outside-scope prefixing, missing choom, omitted foreground/long-lived prefixes.
Existing test_classify_dead_worker_passes_the_run_start changes only to expect the additive worker_pids keyword. Stop-policy scope failure semantics remain intact; continue-policy command-only kills remain non-failures. Retry doubling remains bounded by the existing 12 GiB ceiling and admission; the dispatcher test uses a 2 GiB configured base to verify 4 -> 8 GiB without the ceiling.
